The next lemma collects several properties of the Kronecker product and the $\overline{\mathrm{vec}}(\cdot)$ operator, that will be used throughout the paper. For proofs and further details, we refer to [12].

Lemma 3.

Let $A,A^{\prime},B,B^{\prime}$ be matrices of appropriate dimensions. The following properties hold:

(i) $(A\otimes B)(A^{\prime}\otimes B^{\prime})=(AA^{\prime})\otimes(BB^{\prime})$;

(ii) $(A\otimes B)^{\mkern-1.5mu\scriptstyle\mathsf{T}}=A^{\mkern-1.5mu\scriptstyle\mathsf{T}}\otimes B^{\mkern-1.5mu\scriptstyle\mathsf{T}}$;

(iii) If $A,B\succeq 0$, then for any $s\in\mathbb{R}$ it holds that $(A\otimes B)^{s}=A^{s}\otimes B^{s}$, and in particular, if $A,B\succ 0$ then $(A\otimes B)^{-1}=A^{-1}\otimes B^{-1}$;

(iv) If $A\succeq A^{\prime}$ and $B\succeq B^{\prime}$ then $A\otimes B\succeq A^{\prime}\otimes B^{\prime}$, and in particular, if $A,B\succeq 0$ then $A\otimes B\succeq 0$;

(v) $\trace(A\otimes B)=\trace(A)\trace(B)$;

(vi) $\overline{\mathrm{vec}}(uv^{\mkern-1.5mu\scriptstyle\mathsf{T}})=u\otimes v$ for any two column vectors $u,v$.

