We prove Lemmas 11 and 12. We require several identities involving the $\overline{\mathrm{vec}}(\cdot)$ and $\mathrm{mat}_{i}(\cdot)$ operations, bundled in the following lemma.

Lemma 14.

For any column vectors $u^{1},\ldots,u^{k}$ and order-$k$ tensor $A$ it holds that:

(i) $\overline{\mathrm{vec}}(u^{1}\circ\cdots\circ u^{k})=u^{1}\otimes\cdots\otimes u^{k}$ ;

(ii) $\mathrm{mat}_{i}(u^{1}\circ\cdots\circ u^{k})=u^{i}\big(\bigotimes_{i^{\prime}\neq i}u^{i^{\prime}}\big)^{\mkern-1.5mu\scriptstyle\mathsf{T}}$ ;

(iii) $\overline{\mathrm{vec}}(A)=\overline{\mathrm{vec}}(\mathrm{mat}_{1}(A))=\overline{\mathrm{vec}}(\mathrm{mat}_{k}(A)^{\mkern-1.5mu\scriptstyle\mathsf{T}})$ ;

(iv) $\mathrm{mat}_{i}(A\times_{i}M)=M\mathrm{mat}_{i}(A)$ .

